CORE
main.ii
--winx64 --cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 10 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ ofstream from string converts: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
cpp11_ofstream_from_string preprocessed with the MSVC STL of VS 2022
(14.44.35207, CI artifact), with definitions of memcpy, memmove, memcmp,
memset and strlen inserted before main: on Linux, --winx64 has no bodies
for them.  It used to need about 9 GB and 370 s and report 353 failed
properties: the target of basic_ofstream(const string &)'s delegation did
not construct the virtual base basic_ios ([class.base.init]/6-7), and the
runtime's locale::id::_Id_cnt was nondeterministic.  Now 7 s and 263 MB.
--unwind 10: with --unwind 5 the strlen of "out.txt" is cut and the end
of main is unreachable.
